SUMMARY:Virtual REGISTER: Celebrate Marilyn Monroe 100th Birthday Film Fes
 t with Niagara
DESCRIPTION:Experience Toronto\n**Important: When you sign-up\, you will a
 lso need to Register in advance using the link in The Signing Up section**
  to receive the link to the film.\n\nOn **Saturday June 6th**\, **join The
  100 Birthday Film Fest of Marilyn Monroe in Niagara.** This film history 
 program will start with an introduction to the film\, including the histor
 ical context\, plot summary\, and things to look for\, followed by a full 
 screening of the film. You’ll have the opportunity to discuss the film w
 ith your fellow history lovers via **Zoom**. **Register for your virtual l
 ink of this film on Saturday June 6th at 8pm.**\n\n**Marilyn Monroe was bo
 rn 100 years ago - June 1\, 1926\, and Niagara** is a 1953 American noir t
 hriller film directed by Henry Hathaway and produced by Charles Brackett. 
 Brackett also wrote the screenplay alongside Walter Reisch and Richard Bre
 en. Among the top-billed stars are **Marilyn Monroe**\, Joseph Cotten\, an
 d Jean Peters. Denis O'Dea\, and Max Showalter (credited as Casey Adams) a
 re among other stars appearing in the film. Set in Niagara Falls\, the fil
 m tells the story of two couples: one\, a pair of newlyweds on their honey
 moon\, and the other\, a husband and wife whose turbulent marriage is wrac
 ked by jealousy and deceit. Unlike other films noir of the time\, which we
 re typically black-and-white\, Niagara was shot in "three-strip" Technicol
 or (one of the last films to be made at 20th Century Fox in that format\, 
 as a few months later the studio began converting to CinemaScope\, which h
 ad compatibility problems with three-strip but not with Eastmancolor).\n\n
 Niagara was a box office success and received positive reviews from film c
 ritics. It was one of 20th Century Fox's biggest box office hits that year
 . Monroe was given top billing in Niagara\, which elevated her to movie st
 ar status. Monroe's next two films\, Gentlemen Prefer Blondes and How to M
 arry a Millionaire (both 1953)\, were even bigger successes commercially.\
 n\n**COST**: By Donation\, or Free if you're unable to donate. I encourage
  you to please donate to the host.\n\n**SIGNING UP**:\n\n* **Simply RSVP Y
 es and [Register](https://www.eventbrite.com/e/niagara-marilyn-monroe-100t
 h-birthday-film-fest-livestream-tickets-1990292255714?aff=ebdsoporgprofile
 ) here to receive your link to the event.**\n* The registration company wi
 ll send you a confirmation email and two reminder emails with the link pri
 or to start\n* **Start time: at 8pm**\, click on the link provided to join
  the event\n* Length: 2.5 hours\n*\n\nEnjoy and please post your Comments 
 in the event after.\n\nI encourage you to donate to the host via:\n**PayPa
 l**: DCHistoryAndCulture@gmail.com\n**Venmo**: @DCHistoryAndCulture\n**GoF
 undMe**: https://gofund.me/d29491c0\n\nIf you have questions/ need help\, 
 please contact rkelleman@yahoo.com or https://www.eventbrite.com/support/a
 rticles/en_US/Troubleshooting/did-my-email-send-invitations-order-confirma
 tions-reminders?lg=en_US\n\nRSVPs close 1 day prior hoping there will stil
 l be free spots\; cancellations may result in a No Show.
